.TH HAG 3 "May 2025" "Hag 0.1.0" "Hag AI Compute Runtime"
.SH NAME
hag \- High-Performance AI GPU Compute API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <hag/api.h>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Hag is a bare-metal API specifically designed for AI/ML workloads.
It provides a unified, high-performance compute layer that runs on any
modern GPU hardware without requiring vendor-specific closed-source drivers.
.SH API FUNCTIONS
.SS Instance Management
.nf
HagResult hagCreateInstance(const HagInstanceCreateInfo* pCreateInfo,
                            HagInstance* pInstance);
void hagDestroyInstance(HagInstance instance);
.fi
.SS Device Management
.nf
HagResult hagEnumerateDevices(uint32_t* pDeviceCount, HagDevice* pDevices);
HagResult hagGetDeviceProperties(HagDevice device,
                                 HagDeviceProperties* pProperties);
HagResult hagCreateDevice(HagInstance instance,
                          const HagDeviceCreateInfo* pCreateInfo,
                          HagDevice* pDevice);
void hagDestroyDevice(HagDevice device);
.fi
.SS Buffer Management
.nf
HagResult hagCreateBuffer(HagDevice device,
                          const HagBufferCreateInfo* pCreateInfo,
                          HagBuffer* pBuffer);
void hagDestroyBuffer(HagDevice device, HagBuffer buffer);
HagResult hagMapBuffer(HagDevice device, HagBuffer buffer, void** ppData);
void hagUnmapBuffer(HagDevice device, HagBuffer buffer);
.fi
.SS Tensor Management
.nf
HagResult hagCreateTensor(HagDevice device,
                          const HagTensorCreateInfo* pCreateInfo,
                          HagTensor* pTensor);
void hagDestroyTensor(HagDevice device, HagTensor tensor);
.fi
.SS Kernel Management
.nf
HagResult hagCreateKernel(HagDevice device,
                          const HagKernelCreateInfo* pCreateInfo,
                          HagKernel* pKernel);
void hagDestroyKernel(HagDevice device, HagKernel kernel);
.fi
.SS Command Submission
.nf
HagResult hagCreateCmdBuffer(HagDevice device,
                             const HagCmdBufferCreateInfo* pCreateInfo,
                             HagCmdBuffer* pCmdBuffer);
HagResult hagBeginCmdBuffer(HagCmdBuffer cmdBuffer, uint32_t flags);
HagResult hagEndCmdBuffer(HagCmdBuffer cmdBuffer);
HagResult hagQueueSubmit(HagQueue queue, uint32_t submitCount,
                         const HagSubmitInfo* pSubmits, HagEvent fence);
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUES
Most Hag functions return a
.B HagResult
value indicating success or failure:
.TP
.B HAG_SUCCESS
Operation completed successfully.
.TP
.B HAG_ERROR_OUT_OF_MEMORY
Memory allocation failed.
.TP
.B HAG_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT
An invalid parameter was provided.
.TP
.B HAG_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST
The GPU device became unavailable.
.TP
.B HAG_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED
The requested operation is not supported on this device.
.TP
.B HAG_ERROR_TIMEOUT
An operation timed out.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HAG_LOG_LEVEL
Set the logging level (0=error, 1=warning, 2=info, 3=debug).
.TP
.B HAG_KERNEL_CACHE_DIR
Override the default kernel cache directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/libhag.so
Hag shared library.
.TP
.I /usr/include/hag/api.h
Main API header.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/hag/
User-specific kernel cache and configuration.
